---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data.mjs";
import { polyMailerThicknessOptions } from "../../product-data.mjs";
import { getProductVisual } from "../../product-images.mjs";
import packingSource from "../../assets/new-products/poly-mailers-apparel-packing.jpg";
const packing = await getProductVisual(packingSource);
const path = "/guides/mailer-size-for-clothing/";
const title = "How to Choose the Right Mailer Size for Clothing";
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: title, author: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, publisher: { "@id": `${site.origin}/#organization` }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}${path}`, image: new URL(packing.imageFull, site.origin).toString(), datePublished: "2026-10-20", dateModified: "2026-10-26", inLanguage: "en" };
const breadcrumbs = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", itemListElement: [{ "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: site.origin }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Buying Guides", item: `${site.origin}/guides/` }, { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Clothing mailer size", item: `${site.origin}${path}` }] };
---
<Layout title={`${title} | Welltroy`} description="Measure packed clothing, compare P03, P04 and P05 outer sizes, and distinguish single-wall film thickness from pack thickness. Check fit before approving a mailer." canonicalPath={path} schemas={[schema, breadcrumbs]} ogImage={packing.imageFull} ogImageAlt="Folded clothing being packed into a printed pink poly mailer">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/guides/">Buying Guides</a> / Clothing mailer size</div><p class="eyebrow">Clothing packaging guide</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">Fold and pack the garment as it will ship, then measure packed width, length and thickness. Compare those measurements with candidate mailers, allowing space for insertion and closure. Confirm usable inner dimensions and test a sample before ordering: the catalogue lists outer dimensions.</p><p class="muted">By Welltroy · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-26">26 October 2026</time></p><nav class="anchor-links" aria-label="In this guide"><a href="#measure">Measure</a><a href="#packing-reference">Packing reference</a><a href="#models">Compare models</a><a href="#film-thickness">Thickness units</a><a href="#test">Test the fit</a><a href="#quote">Send a brief</a></nav></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><article class="article-main">
    <h2 id="measure">Measure the Actual Shipping Pack</h2>
    <ol><li>Fold the garment the way your team will pack it. Include any tissue, cardboard insert or <a href="/products/zipper-bags/">inner zipper bag</a> you plan to use.</li><li>Measure the widest width, longest length and greatest thickness of the finished pack. If one mailer will hold several garments, measure the full group.</li><li>Record how the item enters the bag, how much room the adhesive flap needs, and whether it can shift without stressing seams.</li><li>For multiple garment styles, measure the largest packed example for each shipping group rather than assuming one size covers all.</li></ol>
    <div class="guide-callout"><strong>Do not size from a flat garment alone.</strong> Thickness consumes usable space when the mailer wraps around the contents. Seams, lining and flap position reduce the practical opening or closing area. Ask for usable internal measurements for the exact proposed construction.</div>
    <h2 id="packing-reference">A Welltroy Apparel Packing Reference</h2>
    <figure class="packing-reference"><a href={packing.imageFull} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View the apparel packing photograph"><img src={packing.image} srcset={packing.imageSrcSet} sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 40px), 760px" width={packing.imageWidth} height={packing.imageHeight} alt="Folded clothing with inner wrapping being inserted into a pink strawberry-pattern poly mailer" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>Apparel packing photograph supplied by Welltroy. Measure the garment together with the inner wrapping, inserts and other items you will ship.</figcaption></figure>
    <p>The photograph is a packing reference. No model or measured dimensions are assigned to this pictured pack; the numerical example below is illustrative and describes a separate hypothetical item.</p>
    <h2 id="models">Catalogue Example: 24 × 30 × 4 cm Packed Garment</h2>
    <p>This is an illustrative packed item, not a verified Welltroy order. The 2025 catalogue lists the following <a href="/products/poly-mailers/">Poly Mailers</a> dimensions as outer width × length + flap:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Poly mailer catalogue size comparison for clothing"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Catalogue outer size</th><th>What the example suggests</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>P03</td><td>25 × 30 + 5 cm</td><td>Nearly no nominal width or length allowance before 4 cm thickness and seams; do not assume it fits.</td></tr><tr><td>P04</td><td>28 × 37 + 5 cm</td><td>A candidate to check for usable inner space, flap closure and actual packed fit.</td></tr><tr><td>P05</td><td>32 × 40 + 5 cm</td><td>A larger candidate if P04 leaves too little working room; check whether extra space suits your packing process.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p>The “+ 5 cm” is the listed flap, not extra usable body length. These outer figures alone cannot establish fit, and no model above is a guaranteed recommendation. Ask us to confirm inner dimensions, tolerance, closure position, material and availability for the size you intend to order.</p>
    <h2 id="film-thickness">Film Thickness and Packed Thickness Are Different</h2>
    <p><strong>Packed thickness</strong> is the depth of your folded clothing together with its inner packaging. Include it when assessing the room needed inside a mailer. <strong>Film thickness</strong> describes one wall of the bag and is a separate material specification.</p>
    <p>Welltroy's poly mailer reference options are {polyMailerThicknessOptions.map(option => option.microns).join(", ")} μm per side. For example, 60 μm per side is 0.06 mm per side, approximately 2.36 mil per side. It does not describe the depth of a garment pack. Compare the <a href="/products/poly-mailers/#poly-mailer-thickness">single-wall film thickness table</a> and confirm the material, chosen option and tolerance in your quotation.</p>
    <h2 id="test">Test Before Choosing One Size</h2>
    <ul><li>Insert the actual packed garment into a physical sample without forcing it.</li><li>Close the flap in the normal position; check that the adhesive lands securely and contents do not strain the seams.</li><li>Check presentation and movement inside the bag, then test normal fulfillment and shipping handling.</li><li>For rigid or delicate accessories, compare a <a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/">Poly Bubble Mailer</a> or additional protective packaging; test the complete pack.</li></ul>
    <p>For the difference between a plain and cushioned mailer, see <a href="/guides/choose-a-mailer/">Poly Mailers vs Bubble Mailers</a>.</p>
    <p>Keep a <a href="/guides/custom-mailer-sample-approval/#record">sample approval record</a> with the bag model, actual packed dimensions, insertion and closure observations, artwork version and retained sample. If the item mix or packing method changes, repeat the affected fit checks before approving one size for all orders.</p>
    <h2 id="quote">Send Measurements That Can Be Quoted</h2>
    <p>Tell us the garment type, packed width × length × thickness, items per parcel, candidate model if any, quantity per size and design, desired film and closure, print artwork, destination and target timing. If you do not know the mailer size, send packed item measurements and ask us to compare samples.</p><p>After receiving proposals, use the <a href="/guides/compare-custom-mailer-quotes/">quote comparison worksheet</a> to check that each offer uses the same dimensions, single-wall film thickness and delivery scope.</p><a class="button" href="/quote/?product=poly-mailers#quote-form" data-quote-placement="content">Request a clothing mailer quote</a>
  </article><aside class="side-card"><p class="eyebrow">From the catalogue</p><h2>Related Packaging</h2><div class="guide-options"><a href="/products/poly-mailers/"><strong>Poly Mailers</strong><span>Compare listed models and ask for usable inner space</span></a><a href="/products/zipper-bags/"><strong>Zipper Bags</strong><span>Plan inner packaging before measuring the finished pack</span></a><a href="/products/poly-bubble-mailers/"><strong>Poly Bubble Mailers</strong><span>Consider cushioning for compact, sensitive contents</span></a></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides/custom-packaging-500-pieces/">See the custom quote checklist →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>.article-main{min-width:0}.article-main td{min-width:145px;vertical-align:top}.article-main li{margin:0 0 10px}.packing-reference{margin:28px 0;min-width:0}.packing-reference img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:12px}.packing-reference figcaption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin-top:10px}h2[id]{scroll-margin-top:120px}</style>
